## Verdict

PASS. No blocking findings. Four Nit findings, all recorded with an owner.

## Contract check (spec.md amendment 2026-11-01, decision 2, points 1-6, Forge notes (a) and (b))

1. The Muse flow delivers the week 1 list rows. Met: the writer takes list rows plus the approval
   list. T153 proves one job per approved row.
2. One `manifest.json` in the 11a06b9c shape at the batch root, one entry per clean row. Met. T152
   proves the shape and exactly one manifest at the delivery root.
3. `job.id` = the picture-list row id. Met. T153 proves it.
4. `candidate.file` = `<row id>-v1.png`, `lineArt.file` = `<row id>-line-v1.png`; copies of the
   approved Muse prints; originals kept. Met. T154, T155, and T158 prove names, bytes, and SHA-256.
5. The folder prefix is free. Met: the writer delivers bare names at the root; the manifest uses
   directory `w01` only to group batch hashes; the test resolves files by name part.
6. Only clean rows go into the manifest. Met: an unapproved row gets no job (T153), and a failing
   review verdict refuses the whole delivery.

Forge note (a): class A and B at 4000 x 3000, class C at 1500 x 1500. Met through
`planPictureRow` and `PICTURE_SIZES`. T156 proves all three classes and the refusal text names the
row.

Forge note (b): only Kimi reviews in `reviews.kimi`; no invented person review. Met: the mapper
copies only the Kimi entry and a named person entry; the strict zod schema rejects extra review
keys. T159 proves the mapping and the empty `reviews` object.

## Failure atomicity

Every check runs before the first write. The writer collects problems and throws before `mkdir`,
the copies, and the manifest write. A refusal on row 5 leaves no copies, no folder, and no
manifest. T156 and T157 prove the claim for size and gray-pixel refusals.

## Determinism

The manifest text depends on row order, canonical batch file order, and approval-list strings.
`checkedAt` values come from the list, not the wall clock. T161 proves a byte-identical second run.

## Review mapping, CLI, callers, test meaning

- A failing Kimi or person verdict lands in problems and refuses the batch. No unclean row ships.
- The `deliver` command requires all four flags; a live run with no flags exits 1 with the usage
  error. It reads the list read-only and logs its SHA-256. It pins no list hash by design.
- The `rowCaptureJob` export is one additive word; the internal caller is unchanged; owned tsc
  errors are 0.
- T152 to T161 run the real writer against real sharp fixtures on real temporary folders. No mock
  of the code under test.

## Green-log gaps judged

- Write-order mutation: a real coverage gap. The code writes the manifest last by statement order
  only. Nit F1, owner Green.
- `lineArt.renderEvidenceFile` is the empty string: accepted. The interface has no minimum, no zod
  manifest schema exists, and `verifyManifest` never reads the field. Not a defect.
- No class B calm-top or class C white-corner check on Muse prints: out of scope for this task
  pair. Nit F3, owner the Phase 3 delivery task and the PM contract.
- T142/T147 pin list v3 against Workbooks v4: out of scope. The 30 week 1 rows are identical in
  v3 and v4, and `deliver` pins no hash. Nit F4, owner the Phase 4 reconciliation task.

